{"title":"BlueTide Seafood","sub":"Own the trucks, or keep paying a logistics firm?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Food distribution","geo":"United States","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Make vs buy · utilisation · hidden costs and benefits","prompt":"BlueTide distributes frozen seafood to restaurants and grocers along the US East Coast. A logistics company (a 3PL) does all its refrigerated trucking for $2.40 a loaded mile. The COO wants to buy BlueTide's own fleet of 40 refrigerated trucks. The CEO asks you whether owning is cheaper, and whether it's the right move.","clarify":[{"q":"Volume?","a":"About 4.4 million loaded miles a year."},{"q":"Fleet costs?","a":"Trucks cost $180k each and last six years. Drivers cost $95k per truck a year. Fuel and maintenance $0.95 a mile. Insurance and admin $0.6M a year."},{"q":"Return trips?","a":"Trucks come back mostly empty: empty miles add about 35% to the loaded miles. The 3PL charges only for loaded miles because it fills return trips with other customers' freight."},{"q":"Could BlueTide sell its empty return capacity?","a":"Probably about half of it, to other shippers, at about $1.60 a mile."},{"q":"Quality?","a":"About 1.2% of cargo value spoils in transit with the 3PL, through temperature failures. BlueTide ships $150M of product a year."}],"structure":{"root":"Should BlueTide run its own fleet?","branches":[{"head":"3PL cost","items":["Loaded miles × rate"]},{"head":"Own-fleet cost","items":["Trucks (depreciation)","Drivers","Fuel and maintenance, including empty miles","Insurance and admin"]},{"head":"Offsets","items":["Selling return capacity","Less spoilage"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Utilisation","Running a fleet is not our core skill"]}]},"hypothesis":"On loaded miles alone owning looks cheaper, but empty return trips could wipe that out. Spoilage could be the deciding factor, since seafood is valuable.","questions":[{"q":"Compare yearly cost: 3PL vs own fleet, counting only loaded miles.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>3PL: 4.4M × $2.40 = <b>$10.56M</b>.</p> <p>Own fleet: depreciation $7,200k ÷ 6 = $1.2M; drivers 40 × $95k = $3.8M; fuel and maintenance 4.4M × $0.95 = $4.18M; admin $0.6M. Total <b>$9.78M</b>.</p> <p>Owning looks $0.78M a year cheaper.</p>"},{"q":"Now include the empty return miles.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"377.736719pt\" height=\"193.048pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 377.736719 193.048\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 193.048 L 377.736719 193.048 L 377.736719 0 L 0 0 L 0 193.048 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 24.576719 159.456 L 370.536719 159.456 L 370.536719 9.768 L 24.576719 9.768 L 24.576719 159.456 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"60.813636\" y=\"159.456\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(44.144886 174.184) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" d=\"M 493 4083 Q 448 4128 493 4179 Q 691 4397 924 4537 Q 1158 4678 1420 4745 Q 1683 4813 1971 4813 Q 2470 4813 2825 4656 Q 3181 4499 3376 4227 Q 3571 3955 3571 3610 Q 3571 3264 3356 2985 Q 3142 2707 2758 2573 Q 2688 2547 2688 2528 Q 2688 2509 2758 2483 Q 3021 2413 3241 2249 Q 3462 2086 3590 1849 Q 3718 1613 3718 1312 Q 3718 915 3513 601 Q 3309 288 2902 112 Q 2496 -64 1888 -64 Q 1568 -64 1280 9 Q 992 83 745 236 Q 499 390 288 614 Q 262 646 268 672 Q 275 698 307 723 L 582 941 Q 627 973 646 966 Q 666 960 685 941 Q 877 742 1069 627 Q 1261 512 1472 457 Q 1683 403 1933 403 Q 2496 403 2