63 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(115.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(136.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(201.609375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(118.300802 23.552626) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\" d=\"M 3174 2259 Q 3174 2176 3072 2176 L 480 2170 Q 435 2170 416 2189 Q 397 2208 397 2246 L 397 2522 Q 397 2598 454 2598 L 3110 2598 Q 3174 2598 3174 2534 L 3174 2259 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" d=\"M 3456 4749 Q 3507 4749 3532 4723 Q 3558 4698 3552 4672 L 3546 4442 Q 3546 4390 3520 4329 Q 3494 4269 3456 4211 Q 3200 3827 2960 3385 Q 2720 2944 2515 2477 Q 2310 2010 2147 1571 Q 1984 1133 1875 758 Q 1766 384 1728 122 Q 1715 0 1632 0 L 1126 0 Q 1024 0 1050 109 Q 1139 467 1289 918 Q 1440 1370 1661 1891 Q 1882 2413 2182 2982 Q 2483 3552 2861 4147 Q 2886 4186 2880 4211 Q 2874 4237 2816 4237 L 339 4237 Q 262 4237 262 4314 L 307 4685 Q 314 4749 403 4749 L 3456 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(124.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(145.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(205.3125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(187.392344 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\" d=\"M 3174 2259 Q 3174 2176 3072 2176 L 480 2170 Q 435 2170 416 2189 Q 397 2208 397 2246 L 397 2522 Q 397 2598 454 2598 L 3110 2598 Q 3174 2598 3174 2534 L 3174 2259 z\nM 1664 998 Q 1574 998 1574 1101 L 1568 3693 Q 1568 3744 1587 3760 Q 1606 3776 1645 3776 L 1920 3776 Q 1997 3776 1997 3718 L 2003 1062 Q 2003 998 1939 998 L 1664 998 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(123.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(188.015625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(256.043885 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(123.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(183.015625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(324.239802 30.528427) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(115.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(136.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(205 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pe8e73c4ddb\"><rect x=\"24.576719\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · From 3PL cost to own-fleet cost ($M a year)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Empty miles: 35% × 4.4M = 1.54M, costing $1.46M. Own fleet: <b>$11.24M</b>, now <b>$0.68M more</b> than the 3PL.</p> <p>If BlueTide sells half its return capacity to other shippers at $1.60 a mile, it earns $1.23M: net cost $10.01M, $0.55M cheaper than the 3PL.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> on transport cost alone, owning saves only about 5%, and only if half the return trips are filled. That is a thin, fragile margin.</p>"},{"q":"BlueTide's own trucks would carry temperature sensors with live alerts, cutting spoilage to about 0.5%. What does that change?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Spoilage saving: $150M × (1.2% − 0.5%) = <b>$1.05M a year</b>, more than any difference in transport cost.</p> <p>Total yearly gain from owning: <b>$1.60M</b>. Cash payback on the $7.2M fleet: $7.2M ÷ ($1.60M gain + $1.2M non-cash depreciation) = <b>2.6 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the case for owning is about product quality, not trucking cost. That raises a question: could the 3PL fit the same sensors for less?</p>"},{"q":"What would you recommend, and what would you check first?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Ask the 3PL to commit to sensor monitoring and a spoilage penalty in its contract. If it agrees, most of the gain comes without owning trucks.</li> <li>If not, build a fleet for the core, predictable routes and keep the 3PL for peaks and long-haul.</li> <li>Check: the 1.2% spoilage figure, how reliably return loads can be sold, and driver availability.</li></ul>"}],"reco":"On trucking cost alone, owning a fleet saves only about 5% once empty return trips are counted, and only if BlueTide can sell half its return capacity. The real prize is spoilage: better temperature control saves about $1.05M a year. First, ask the 3PL to fit sensors and accept a spoilage penalty, which captures most of that gain without $7.2M of trucks. If it won't, buy a fleet for the core routes and keep the 3PL for peaks (a full 40-truck fleet would gain about $1.60M a year, cash payback 2.6 years; a smaller fleet scales this down). Risk: running a fleet is a new skill. Next step: verify spoilage by route.","great":["Builds the own-fleet cost line by line","Catches the empty-return-mile trap","Finds that spoilage outweighs trucking cost","Looks for a way to get the benefit without the asset"],"id":54,"slug":"bluetide-seafood"}